    "why": "Two earlier attempts at the DeepSeek-V4-Flash run are kept because their failure mode is the point, not the score. ds4-server v0.5.4 refused requests mid-run with HTTP 503: 'serial right-size: no graph fits (prompt=N need_min=N+1024); refusing 503'. The harness sends session-less requests; the server sized the graph by estimate and refused when unsure. Updating to v0.6.2 — which measures the graph instead of estimating it, and allocates the session graph lazily — removed the refusals entirely.",
